1
00:00:28,560 --> 00:00:29,980
Violin's You

2
00:00:40,080 --> 00:00:43,300
I don't know.

3
00:01:30,080 --> 00:01:31,160
Let's go.

4
00:01:59,980 --> 00:02:01,060
Oh, my God.

5
00:02:39,420 --> 00:02:40,250
Let's go.

6
00:03:39,100 --> 00:03:41,860
Now, where the hell is he?

7
00:03:53,420 --> 00:03:55,060
What is it you need?

8
00:04:00,760 --> 00:04:02,240
What do you need? Lordeo!

9
00:04:17,060 --> 00:04:19,580
Whole Horse, what is it you need?

10
00:04:22,480 --> 00:04:23,310
I...

11
00:04:23,393 --> 00:04:24,280
got a report.

12
00:04:27,940 --> 00:04:29,060
A report?

13
00:04:29,380 --> 00:04:34,900
That guy Polnareff, you see, he done
gone and defected to Joestar's outfit.

14
00:04:35,120 --> 00:04:36,360
My dear whole horse,

15
00:04:36,620 --> 00:04:41,220
the actions Polnareff chooses are
of very little consequence to me.

16
00:04:42,120 --> 00:04:46,473
After all, errand boys are easy to
come by, wouldn't you say, whole horse?

17
00:04:46,900 --> 00:04:49,097
You've wasted my time coming here.

18
00:04:49,180 --> 00:04:51,097
And my time is very valuable.

19
00:04:51,180 --> 00:04:54,220
Now run along, you still have work to do.

20
00:04:57,880 --> 00:05:01,477
First and foremost, do hurry up with
the termination of the Joestars.

21
00:05:01,560 --> 00:05:04,677
And this time, try not to disappoint me.

22
00:05:04,760 --> 00:05:07,697
How dare you tell me to live
up to your expectations?

23
00:05:07,780 --> 00:05:09,877
Just who do you think you are anyway?

24
00:05:09,960 --> 00:05:12,837
Just look at you, sitting
there with your back to me?

25
00:05:12,920 --> 00:05:14,737
Leaving yourself wide open!

26
00:05:14,820 --> 00:05:18,114
Heh, everyone's just blowing
your rip out of proportion.

27
00:05:18,360 --> 00:05:21,340
I never pledged eternal
loyalties to kiss my ass.

28
00:05:31,220 --> 00:05:32,620
Adios, Dio.

29
00:05:32,840 --> 00:05:35,000
You can regret this moment in hell.

30
00:05:42,200 --> 00:05:43,030
What the?

31
00:05:43,940 --> 00:05:44,770
Ah,

32
00:05:44,853 --> 00:05:46,357
even at the moment of the kill,

33
00:05:46,440 --> 00:05:49,717
your breathing is measured
and you perspire very little.

34
00:05:49,800 --> 00:05:51,340
Not bad, whole horse.

35
00:05:52,440 --> 00:05:53,960
Not bad at all.

36
00:05:58,860 --> 00:05:59,940
What the hell?

37
00:06:00,180 --> 00:06:02,480
How did he get behind me?

38
00:06:08,380 --> 00:06:09,210
I...

39
00:06:09,293 --> 00:06:10,780
I just don't get it.

40
00:06:15,000 --> 00:06:15,830
I don't...

41
00:06:15,913 --> 00:06:17,720
I just don't get it!

42
00:06:27,740 --> 00:06:30,940
Why would I have a dream
like that right now?

43
00:06:52,240 --> 00:06:55,317
If we continue at the rate at
which we're currently traveling,

44
00:06:55,400 --> 00:06:58,812
we should make it to the Red
Sea in just a couple of days.

45
00:07:00,340 --> 00:07:06,740
Here's where we are and once we pass
right through there we'll be in Egypt?

46
00:07:10,100 --> 00:07:12,140
Every day we're getting closer!

47
00:07:14,880 --> 00:07:16,400
Sorry to make you wait.

48
00:07:19,440 --> 00:07:23,277
Let's go uh Mr Joestar who
is that you were talking to?

49
00:07:23,360 --> 00:07:26,840
Oh that was just my friend in Egypt.

50
00:07:28,220 --> 00:07:32,137
In any case, it's already been more
than 30 days since we left Japan.

51
00:07:32,220 --> 00:07:34,691
There's no time to wait, so let's move on.

52
00:07:34,800 --> 00:07:35,800
Ah, that's right.

53
00:07:50,680 --> 00:07:55,280
Little lady, you're more beautiful
and breathtaking than a desert rose.

54
00:07:56,460 --> 00:07:57,560
Whole horse.

55
00:08:01,140 --> 00:08:03,740
Heck, I never imagined that you, yourself,

56
00:08:04,140 --> 00:08:10,740
would be the one to come all the way
down here to meet with this old cowpoke.

57
00:08:11,320 --> 00:08:13,837
Hey, hey, now don't you go
looking at me like that.

58
00:08:13,920 --> 00:08:17,197
If you and I were to become partners,
well, hell, we'd be unbeatable.

59
00:08:17,280 --> 00:08:18,633
Come on, let's look up.

60
00:08:21,260 --> 00:08:22,920
You are so cold.

61
00:08:24,160 --> 00:08:24,990
Hmm?

62
00:08:25,073 --> 00:08:25,903
Hmm?

63
00:08:26,420 --> 00:08:27,250
Shit!

64
00:08:27,340 --> 00:08:29,634
What in the name of hell are you doing?

65
00:08:30,240 --> 00:08:34,100
So, why do you suppose you were
asked to come here homeless?

66
00:08:34,600 --> 00:08:41,400
Lord Dio has granted me this opportunity
to avenge the death of my son, J. Guile.

67
00:08:43,660 --> 00:08:44,520
Avenge him?

68
00:08:45,300 --> 00:08:47,140
How dare you abandon J.

69
00:08:47,340 --> 00:08:50,046
Guile and shamelessly
make your way back here?

70
00:08:50,860 --> 00:08:52,740
Hey now, just hold on there.

71
00:08:52,900 --> 00:08:54,197
Listen, you got it all wrong.

72
00:08:54,280 --> 00:08:55,457
By the time I arrived, J.

73
00:08:55,540 --> 00:08:56,893
Guile was already dead.

74
00:08:57,320 --> 00:08:58,740
Stop making excuses!

75
00:08:59,220 --> 00:09:02,080
You shall atone for the
crime of abandoning J.

76
00:09:02,300 --> 00:09:03,860
Guile by your death!

77
00:09:06,480 --> 00:09:10,860
You too must have heard rumors,
but have never seen my stand.

78
00:09:15,580 --> 00:09:17,837
Yes, let me show it to you, whole horse.

79
00:09:17,920 --> 00:09:19,660
No, no way.

80
00:09:19,920 --> 00:09:21,214
You're not going to...

81
00:09:21,760 --> 00:09:23,620
My stand. Justice.

82
00:09:24,760 --> 00:09:25,590
Justice?

83
00:09:31,760 --> 00:09:32,590
What?

84
00:09:32,860 --> 00:09:34,660
What's this? Mist?

85
00:09:34,920 --> 00:09:37,060
Yes, a mist of death.

86
00:09:37,740 --> 00:09:38,570
Death?

87
00:09:40,420 --> 00:09:42,160
What the hell?

88
00:09:47,920 --> 00:09:51,420
Hmm, a clean hole has opened now.

89
00:09:52,020 --> 00:09:56,020
Yes, my stand, Justice,
is a stand of mist.

90
00:09:56,860 --> 00:10:00,860
Whatever wound this mist touches
will end up with a hole like that.

91
00:10:02,220 --> 00:10:04,080
Go dance with Justice.

92
00:10:07,220 --> 00:10:09,820
Cut this shit off or I get mad.

93
00:10:13,820 --> 00:10:15,820
Enough is enough.

94
00:10:19,780 --> 00:10:26,440
You see, when the mist enters the
hole, it turns you into a puppet.

95
00:10:33,420 --> 00:10:37,100
Die by your own stand, whole horse.

96
00:10:45,260 --> 00:10:46,620
Justice prevails.

97
00:11:00,580 --> 00:11:03,117
Polnareff, are you able to
see well enough to drive?

98
00:11:03,200 --> 00:11:05,788
I've never seen such a
thick blanket of fog.

99
00:11:06,160 --> 00:11:09,454
Yeah, it's getting pretty
hard to see the road up ahead.

100
00:11:10,660 --> 00:11:11,490
That's odd.

101
00:11:11,640 --> 00:11:13,464
It's only about three o 'clock.

102
00:11:13,660 --> 00:11:14,737
We have no choice.

103
00:11:14,820 --> 00:11:18,517
Let's stop in the next town and
look for a place to spend the night.

104
00:11:18,600 --> 00:11:19,430
Sounds good.

105
00:11:50,820 --> 00:11:53,060
Something strange about this town.

106
00:11:53,300 --> 00:11:54,460
It's too quiet.

107
00:11:54,760 --> 00:11:56,584
This place gives me the creeps.

108
00:11:57,680 --> 00:11:59,240
Hey, Jotaro!

109
00:12:01,080 --> 00:12:03,020
Oh, I guess you're right.

110
00:12:04,440 --> 00:12:06,540
No point in just standing around.

111
00:12:07,180 --> 00:12:09,380
Well then, let's go find a hotel.

112
00:12:11,240 --> 00:12:14,220
Come on, doesn't anyone live in this town?

113
00:12:15,840 --> 00:12:17,781
We can't even ask for directions.

114
00:12:20,220 --> 00:12:22,200
Someone dumped a dead dog there.

115
00:12:24,140 --> 00:12:25,260
That's disgusting!

116
00:12:25,680 --> 00:12:26,600
What a smell!

117
00:12:27,300 --> 00:12:29,880
Oh, there's someone now! Hey, mister!

118
00:12:30,400 --> 00:12:32,677
Excuse me, but we're looking for a hotel.

119
00:12:32,760 --> 00:12:36,137
Can we find a hotel with clean
bathrooms somewhere around here?

120
00:12:36,220 --> 00:12:40,457
Really sorry to bother you while you're
napping, but could you wake up for a second?

121
00:12:40,540 --> 00:12:41,370
Ah!

122
00:12:41,453 --> 00:12:42,360
This guy is dead!

123
00:12:42,720 --> 00:12:44,955
Why is he out on the street like this?

124
00:12:45,040 --> 00:12:47,537
Could it be an accident or a heart attack?

125
00:12:47,620 --> 00:12:48,520
It's possible.

126
00:12:48,820 --> 00:12:52,537
But I don't think it's as simple
as some guy having a heart attack.

127
00:12:52,620 --> 00:12:55,617
Why don't you pull his hand
out where we can see it?

128
00:12:55,700 --> 00:12:56,530
Okay.

129
00:12:58,680 --> 00:12:59,510
Whoa!

130
00:13:03,220 --> 00:13:04,050
Oh!

131
00:13:08,000 --> 00:13:14,020
The gun is still warm, which means not
much time has passed since it was fired.

132
00:13:14,440 --> 00:13:15,940
So he shot himself then?

133
00:13:16,640 --> 00:13:18,800
But where's the wound? Right here.

134
00:13:19,000 --> 00:13:22,417
There's a hole underneath this guy's
throat the size of a ping-pong ball.

135
00:13:22,500 --> 00:13:24,088
Is that the cause of death?

136
00:13:24,900 --> 00:13:26,200
So where's the blood?

137
00:13:26,460 --> 00:13:29,237
A wound like that should
have gushed blood like crazy,

138
00:13:29,320 --> 00:13:31,085
leaving a big pool all around.

139
00:13:31,360 --> 00:13:32,357
Normally, anyway.

140
00:13:32,440 --> 00:13:34,860
Th-that's not all. Look at this.

141
00:13:35,000 --> 00:13:37,420
I've never seen anything like it. Hm?

142
00:13:38,720 --> 00:13:40,880
Wh-what happened to this dead body?

143
00:13:42,040 --> 00:13:44,360
There are holes all over this man.

144
00:13:44,480 --> 00:13:46,917
And not a trace of blood
from any of the wounds.

145
00:13:47,000 --> 00:13:48,588
Why was he killed this way?

146
00:13:48,780 --> 00:13:50,427
Is there some meaning to it?

147
00:13:50,940 --> 00:13:51,770
Shit!

148
00:13:51,900 --> 00:13:54,637
Someone tell me what the
hell is going on here!

149
00:13:54,720 --> 00:13:56,014
Just calm down, Polar.

150
00:13:58,600 --> 00:14:01,360
In any case, we have to get the police.

151
00:14:03,420 --> 00:14:04,660
Madam, excuse me.

152
00:14:04,840 --> 00:14:05,877
We need your help.

153
00:14:05,960 --> 00:14:07,357
We need you to call the police.

154
00:14:07,440 --> 00:14:09,677
There's a man lying dead in the street.

155
00:14:09,760 --> 00:14:11,140
Excuse me. Hello.

156
00:14:11,600 --> 00:14:12,437
Can't you hear me?

157
00:14:12,520 --> 00:14:13,820
Are you talking to me?

158
00:14:15,840 --> 00:14:17,300
What is it you want?

159
00:14:17,540 --> 00:14:20,820
Oh, yes, there's a dead man
over there in the street.

160
00:14:21,020 --> 00:14:24,020
We need you to call the
police as soon as possible.

161
00:14:24,200 --> 00:14:25,460
Ah, a man.

162
00:14:25,940 --> 00:14:26,940
I see.

163
00:14:28,800 --> 00:14:31,980
So, you want me to
report it to the police?

164
00:14:32,560 --> 00:14:34,340
Ah, so itchy.

165
00:14:36,060 --> 00:14:37,337
If you would, madam.

166
00:14:37,420 --> 00:14:39,420
We'd appreciate it if you'd hurry.

167
00:14:40,380 --> 00:14:41,980
What's going on, anyway?

168
00:14:42,340 --> 00:14:46,869
There seems to be something very wrong
with the people in this town, old man.

169
00:14:47,040 --> 00:14:51,275
You know, I'm wondering if this could
be the work of another stand user.

170
00:14:51,520 --> 00:14:52,579
What do you think?

171
00:14:52,960 --> 00:14:53,790
Perhaps,

172
00:14:53,873 --> 00:14:57,137
but I have no idea what our
pursuers would gain by murdering

173
00:14:57,220 --> 00:15:00,279
an innocent man before we
even arrived in this town.

174
00:15:00,680 --> 00:15:02,327
I just don't see the motive.

175
00:15:02,440 --> 00:15:04,557
We shouldn't ignore the
possibility, though.

176
00:15:04,640 --> 00:15:06,581
His death is just too damn weird.

177
00:15:07,540 --> 00:15:10,040
Jostar-san, I have to agree with Jotaro.

178
00:15:10,340 --> 00:15:14,857
If he's right and there's a stand user
hiding here, we are in serious danger.

179
00:15:14,940 --> 00:15:17,557
And in that case, we need to
get out of here right away.

180
00:15:17,640 --> 00:15:20,117
Are you suggesting we try
to escape in this fog?

181
00:15:20,200 --> 00:15:22,141
Now that is what I call suicidal!

182
00:15:22,280 --> 00:15:23,797
Then what are we supposed to do?

183
00:15:23,880 --> 00:15:25,821
Well, how the hell should I know?

184
00:15:26,360 --> 00:15:28,520
Both of you, just calm down.

185
00:15:28,800 --> 00:15:30,447
What's the point of arguing?

186
00:15:50,640 --> 00:15:56,340
So it must be here, a dead person,

187
00:15:56,740 --> 00:15:59,880
I have brought you the police. Yeah!

188
00:16:00,220 --> 00:16:03,808
I'm so glad there are some normal
people living in this town!

189
00:16:04,060 --> 00:16:06,080
Huh, so it seems, Polnareff.

190
00:16:07,080 --> 00:16:10,460
From what I see, I
presume you are travelers.

191
00:16:10,860 --> 00:16:15,660
But with this fog, I'm afraid it's
too dangerous to drive out of town.

192
00:16:16,020 --> 00:16:18,240
I happen to manage a nearby hotel.

193
00:16:18,720 --> 00:16:22,308
I think you'd find it a comfortable
place to spend the night.

194
00:16:23,020 --> 00:16:23,850
Yeah!

195
00:16:23,933 --> 00:16:24,763
A total godsend!

196
00:16:24,846 --> 00:16:25,676
That's what you are!

197
00:16:25,759 --> 00:16:26,589
This is great.

198
00:16:26,672 --> 00:16:27,502
We need a hotel.

199
00:16:27,940 --> 00:16:29,897
Hey, everybody, can we stay there?

200
00:16:29,980 --> 00:16:30,810
Huh?

201
00:16:30,893 --> 00:16:31,723
Can we?

202
00:16:31,860 --> 00:16:32,742
Hmm, all right.

203
00:16:33,920 --> 00:16:35,880
What do you two think about that?

204
00:16:48,060 --> 00:16:51,060
My word, those police
officers are certainly rough.

205
00:16:51,320 --> 00:16:52,937
Yeah, what's with that attitude?

206
00:16:53,020 --> 00:16:55,757
You'd think there were dead bodies
on every street corner around here.

207
00:16:55,840 --> 00:16:56,670
Unbelievable.

208
00:16:56,753 --> 00:17:01,437
Well well my dear guests shall we get

209
00:17:01,520 --> 00:17:04,817
going to the fog is very dense please.

210
00:17:04,900 --> 00:17:09,157
Follow me so you don't
get lost hey old lady

211
00:17:09,240 --> 00:17:12,877
wait up please don't
forget your Luggage we're

212
00:17:12,960 --> 00:17:17,197
leaving now are you
ready anytime we're just

213
00:17:17,280 --> 00:17:20,339
staying for one night So
we don't have much luggage.

214
00:17:30,620 --> 00:17:32,920
Well, well, we have arrived.

215
00:17:33,300 --> 00:17:34,560
This is my hotel.

216
00:17:35,580 --> 00:17:38,940
Here, here, welcoming the party of four.

217
00:17:39,680 --> 00:17:41,360
Come in, come in.

218
00:17:42,720 --> 00:17:43,550
Wow!

219
00:17:45,840 --> 00:17:50,440
I was a little bit worried about what
kind of place that old hag would manage.

220
00:17:50,640 --> 00:17:52,720
But this is a real find.

221
00:17:52,880 --> 00:17:54,240
Yes, so it would seem.

222
00:17:55,320 --> 00:17:58,780
Please, sign right here, Mr. Joestar.

223
00:17:59,580 --> 00:18:03,680
Old lady, just now you used the
name Joestar to refer to him.

224
00:18:03,980 --> 00:18:06,080
Tell me, how do you know that name?

225
00:18:11,460 --> 00:18:13,760
Oh, please, my dear guest.

226
00:18:13,980 --> 00:18:15,940
He was addressed earlier as Mr.

227
00:18:16,060 --> 00:18:17,240
Joestar by him,

228
00:18:18,080 --> 00:18:22,300
that gentleman right over
there. Huh? Who, me? Hmm.

229
00:18:23,540 --> 00:18:25,097
Did I say that or didn't I?

230
00:18:25,180 --> 00:18:26,062
Let me see now.

231
00:18:26,320 --> 00:18:28,480
Wait, well, I... But no, wait.

232
00:18:28,720 --> 00:18:30,308
At the time, I thought I...

233
00:18:33,700 --> 00:18:35,697
Hey, you're the one who called him that.

234
00:18:35,780 --> 00:18:37,177
Just because I'm old,

235
00:18:37,260 --> 00:18:40,137
it doesn't mean you can treat me
like I'm going senile, fanget.

236
00:18:40,220 --> 00:18:41,050
Okay, okay.

237
00:18:41,360 --> 00:18:43,360
Yes, I'm sure I said that, Jotaro.

238
00:18:44,300 --> 00:18:45,220
Now I remember.

239
00:18:45,440 --> 00:18:46,969
Yes, of course, of course.

240
00:18:50,200 --> 00:18:51,217
Didn't I tell you?

241
00:18:51,300 --> 00:18:53,417
because you didn't make yourself clear.

242
00:18:53,500 --> 00:18:54,330
My fault.

243
00:18:54,413 --> 00:18:55,243
My fault, old lady.

244
00:18:55,326 --> 00:18:56,156
Really.

245
00:19:00,360 --> 00:19:01,190
Enya.

246
00:19:01,273 --> 00:19:02,103
A woman.

247
00:19:02,840 --> 00:19:05,297
She's been staying with
us since yesterday.

248
00:19:05,380 --> 00:19:07,080
So, what about her?

249
00:19:09,520 --> 00:19:13,814
No, I just thought it was unusual for
a woman to be traveling by herself.

250
00:19:14,000 --> 00:19:15,860
She's a beautiful lady.

251
00:19:16,300 --> 00:19:19,720
Quite a rare occurrence around here. Yeah?

252
00:19:20,060 --> 00:19:21,766
She's that beautiful a woman?

253
00:19:21,880 --> 00:19:25,097
Mmm, I'd definitely love to
get well acquainted with her.

254
00:19:25,180 --> 00:19:26,260
In your dreams.

255
00:19:27,740 --> 00:19:28,570
Hmm.

256
00:19:28,960 --> 00:19:29,790
Hmm.

257
00:19:31,600 --> 00:19:34,780
I regret to mention that only Mr.

258
00:19:35,220 --> 00:19:39,180
Palnareff's room will be
on the second floor. What?

259
00:19:39,360 --> 00:19:41,157
That's really no problem at all.

260
00:19:41,240 --> 00:19:43,637
By the way, I noticed
that ever since we met,

261
00:19:43,720 --> 00:19:45,577
you've only been using your right hand.

262
00:19:45,660 --> 00:19:51,000
And if you don't mind, I'd like to ask,
Um, is something wrong with your left?

263
00:19:53,440 --> 00:19:55,300
Oh, my left hand.

264
00:19:55,620 --> 00:19:56,920
I burned this hand.

265
00:19:57,180 --> 00:19:59,980
I accidentally spilled hot water on it.

266
00:20:02,580 --> 00:20:03,620
I see.

267
00:20:03,980 --> 00:20:06,580
You really should be
more careful, old lady.

268
00:20:08,560 --> 00:20:09,877
Yes, thank you.

269
00:20:09,960 --> 00:20:12,240
From now on, I will be more careful.

270
00:20:14,880 --> 00:20:17,420
What was that about earlier, Jotaro?

271
00:20:19,020 --> 00:20:23,432
We can't tell who might be an enemy,
so I thought I'd ask a trick question.

272
00:20:24,440 --> 00:20:25,460
Besides, and?

273
00:20:25,920 --> 00:20:28,037
Ever since we arrived in this town,

274
00:20:28,120 --> 00:20:31,532
I've had this feeling that
we're constantly being watched.

275
00:20:31,620 --> 00:20:33,140
Yes, I agree.

276
00:20:33,560 --> 00:20:36,100
A woman from Egypt, a dead body.

277
00:20:36,540 --> 00:20:38,069
Too much of a coincidence.

278
00:20:39,420 --> 00:20:41,160
Oh, room 303.

279
00:20:41,780 --> 00:20:42,877
Hey, this one is mine.

280
00:20:42,960 --> 00:20:44,489
Well, let's talk tomorrow.

281
00:20:54,460 --> 00:20:55,580
Ah, beat!

282
00:20:55,900 --> 00:20:59,135
This bed sure is more
comfortable than that damn truck.

283
00:21:23,260 --> 00:21:24,160
Damn it!

284
00:21:24,460 --> 00:21:27,777
What the hell is up with that
old woman's bandage left hand?

285
00:21:27,860 --> 00:21:29,684
I can't stop thinking about it.

286
00:21:31,400 --> 00:21:33,320
I definitely need a drink.

287
00:21:39,500 --> 00:21:41,900
Oh, yeah. This way.

288
00:21:54,320 --> 00:21:58,760
Hey, that must be the hottie the old
woman in the hotel was talking about.

289
00:22:17,340 --> 00:22:18,960
Barkeep, let's make it two.

290
00:22:19,200 --> 00:22:22,537
A whiskey for me and another
for the lady while you're at it.

291
00:22:22,620 --> 00:22:24,620
The name is Jean-Pierre Polnareff.

292
00:22:24,780 --> 00:22:26,897
Are you here on a sightseeing
trip with friends?

293
00:22:26,980 --> 00:22:31,197
Or might you be traveling alone, looking
for someone to spend some time with?

294
00:22:31,280 --> 00:22:33,040
My name is...

295
00:22:34,180 --> 00:22:35,010
Enya.

296
00:22:47,680 --> 00:22:48,510
Strange.

297
00:22:48,720 --> 00:22:51,485
It feels like we've
entered a city of the dead.

298
00:22:57,660 --> 00:22:58,490
Who's there?

299
00:23:02,080 --> 00:23:03,180
No one there.

300
00:23:03,460 --> 00:23:05,460
Felt like someone was watching me.

301
00:23:24,780 --> 00:23:28,280
I'm traveling in search of a person.

302
00:23:29,200 --> 00:23:33,040
Well, uh, I'd be happy to
help you in any way I can.

303
00:23:34,860 --> 00:23:36,540
I'm looking for a killer.

304
00:23:38,440 --> 00:23:39,460
A killer?

305
00:23:43,340 --> 00:23:44,170
Whoa!

306
00:23:44,253 --> 00:23:45,083
What are the chances?

307
00:23:45,166 --> 00:23:47,497
I've been out traveling on the
road looking for a killer, too!

308
00:23:47,580 --> 00:23:48,580
Oh, that's weird.

309
00:23:51,260 --> 00:23:54,848
I've been searching for someone
who brutally murdered my son.

310
00:23:55,960 --> 00:23:57,820
My own flesh and blood.

311
00:24:04,260 --> 00:24:05,300
I understand.

312
00:24:05,800 --> 00:24:07,520
I understand how you feel.

313
00:24:08,220 --> 00:24:12,160
Well, somebody, some sick bastard
murdered my younger sister.

314
00:24:14,140 --> 00:24:16,320
I'll help you find that killer, Enya.

315
00:24:20,040 --> 00:24:20,870
What the?

316
00:24:23,400 --> 00:24:24,320
Wait a minute.

317
00:24:24,580 --> 00:24:25,698
That's Whole Horse.

318
00:24:25,960 --> 00:24:27,880
What the hell is he doing here?

319
00:24:32,420 --> 00:24:33,460
What's going on?

320
00:24:38,940 --> 00:24:40,528
What is this guy's problem?

321
00:24:41,320 --> 00:24:43,026
I've got nothing against you.

322
00:24:52,940 --> 00:24:55,460
Something really strange is going on here.

323
00:24:55,740 --> 00:24:58,180
That bartender is no ordinary human.

324
00:24:58,440 --> 00:25:00,146
Why was he trying to kill me?

325
00:25:04,500 --> 00:25:05,794
What is it, Miss Enya?

326
00:25:07,720 --> 00:25:10,260
I didn't finish my story yet, did I?

327
00:25:10,740 --> 00:25:14,020
But you see, I've actually
already found the killer.

328
00:25:23,000 --> 00:25:25,317
You're the man who was dead in
the middle of the street today.

329
00:25:25,400 --> 00:25:27,694
I saw your wounds with my own two eyes.

330
00:25:27,800 --> 00:25:29,477
How is it you can still be alive?

331
00:25:29,560 --> 00:25:31,700
The killer is you, Polareff.

332
00:25:33,120 --> 00:25:36,157
You have been a thorn in
the sight of Lord Dio.

333
00:25:36,240 --> 00:25:39,300
And you are the killer of my son, J. Gile.

334
00:25:39,640 --> 00:25:40,580
Your son?

335
00:25:40,980 --> 00:25:43,420
You gave birth to that murdering bastard?

336
00:25:43,720 --> 00:25:46,779
I take it you've got your
own special kind of stand?

337
00:25:52,420 --> 00:25:54,920
There can only be one stand per person.

338
00:25:55,780 --> 00:26:01,557
But you see, my stand of the mist, the
stand of justice, controls the dead.

339
00:26:01,640 --> 00:26:07,200
Hundreds and thousands are at my disposal
to do as I say, the moment I say it.

340
00:26:08,980 --> 00:26:13,540
See how my beloved clamor for
your attention, Polnareff?

341
00:26:14,420 --> 00:26:18,980
And since they're already
dead, you can't kill them.

342
00:26:28,440 --> 00:26:29,777
Now I get it.

343
00:26:29,860 --> 00:26:33,880
How dare you kill my
precious son, you bastard.

344
00:26:34,380 --> 00:26:35,880
You will pay for it.

345
00:26:36,440 --> 00:26:40,180
Die a slow and painful death. Pull around.
